WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
Draw or count repeated tile groups; use the difference to predict the number in later

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:05.491
figures.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:12.912
Figure counts: 4, 7, 10, ... What is figure 7? The answer is 22. Add 3 each time: 4

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.668
plus (7 minus 1) times 3 equals 22.

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:21.848
A tile design during a reading competition has 4, 9, 14, ... tiles in successive

00:00:21.848 --> 00:00:26.453
figures. How many tiles are in figure 9? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:32.835
A tile design during a reading competition has 4, 9, 14, ... tiles in successive

00:00:32.835 --> 00:00:39.868
figures. How many tiles are in figure 9? The answer is 44. Add 5 each time: 4 plus (9

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.089
minus 1) times 5 equals 44.
